        "The Godavari flowed beside Panchavati, its waters moving quietly beneath the shade of ancient trees. The dwelling that Lakshmana had built stood among the trees, simple in appearance but carefully made. Its walls were woven from branches and leaves, and its surroundings had gradually become familiar to the three who lived there. What had once been an unfamiliar stretch of forest had become their home.",
