        "The army of Janasthana emerged from the forest in a vast formation. Chariots moved at the front, followed by warriors carrying bows and weapons. Khara commanded the force, while Dushana and Trishira stood among the principal leaders. The number of warriors was overwhelming, and their confidence was visible in the way they advanced.",
        "Rama stood before them with his bow. He did not retreat toward the dwelling, nor did he attempt to hide from the approaching force. His attention moved across the army, observing its commanders and the direction from which the attack would come.",
