        "Rama replied, 'Your sister came to our dwelling and attempted to harm my wife. My brother stopped her. Your warriors then came to attack us, and I defended myself. You have brought an army against a man who has sought only to live in the forest.'",
        "Khara answered, 'You speak as though you have the right to judge us. You have entered the land of Janasthana and challenged its rulers. Today you will learn the cost of that decision.'",
        "Rama raised his bow. 'I have no desire to harm those who do not threaten the innocent. But I will not allow your army to attack me or those under my protection.'",
        "The rakshasa commanders gave the signal. The first wave of warriors advanced, sending weapons and arrows toward Rama. He answered with a rapid and controlled assault, meeting their attack without allowing them to surround him.",
        "The battle spread across the clearing. Rama moved through the assault with extraordinary skill. His arrows struck the advancing warriors and disrupted their formations. Whenever one group attempted to close in, he turned toward it before it could reach him.",
        "The army had expected its numbers to overwhelm a single prince. Instead, it found itself facing an archer whose precision and composure made every advance costly. Khara watched from his chariot as the first ranks began to fall."
