        "Ravana's interest deepened. He was accustomed to hearing descriptions of beautiful women and had taken pride in possessing what others could only admire. Shurpanakha's words had awakened a desire that was strengthened by the thought that Sita belonged to the prince who had defeated his family.",
        "Shurpanakha continued, 'You should not allow Rama to remain unchallenged. He has destroyed Khara's army and humiliated our family. Take the woman away from him. Let him experience the loss that he has brought upon us.'",
        "Ravana did not answer immediately. He considered the defeat of Janasthana, the strength of Rama, and the woman whose beauty had captured his sister's attention. His thoughts moved beyond the question of revenge.",
        "At last, he said, 'Tell me again where this dwelling stands and how Rama lives there.' Shurpanakha repeated the details of Panchavati, unaware of how firmly her words had taken hold of Ravana's mind."
