        "He knew that Rama was a formidable warrior. A direct assault would be dangerous, and the strength of Janasthana had already been destroyed. Ravana therefore began to seek a method based on deception rather than open battle.",
        "He decided to approach Maricha, a rakshasa who had previously encountered Rama and knew the prince's abilities. Ravana believed that Maricha's knowledge and powers of illusion could help him carry out his intention.",
        "The king prepared to leave Lanka. His decision was no longer simply about answering the defeat of Janasthana. He had chosen to pursue Sita, and he intended to use deception to separate her from Rama."
